{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Correction: the merged SHA is `395761dfbd4fd8e2710d98a3117d2419607e429d`, not the\n`9f95ab706aaf...` recorded in the previous comment. Gerrit's Rebase-If-Necessary submit\nrewrote the commit server-side, so `9f95ab70` was only the local pre-rebase object. The\ntree content is identical; the verification evidence in that comment stands.\n\nThe close was refused, correctly. The landed commit touches 12 files; the recorded\nfile_impact declared 5, and 2 of those named paths that never existed: the test lives at\n`tests/unit/test_plan_review_overlap.py` rather than `tests/test_plan_review_overlap.py`,\nand `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/passes.py` was read but never modified. Six real files were\nundeclared: `.gitignore`, `.rebar/criteria_routing.json`,\n`src/rebar/llm/plan_review/__init__.py`,\n`src/rebar/llm/plan_review/production_batch_runner.py`,\n`src/rebar/llm/workflow/gate_dispatch.py` and\n`src/rebar/llm/workflow/gates/plan-review.yaml`.\n\nWhat drifted is the structured field, not the plan. The Approach section names 5 of those\n6 explicitly and describes the edit each one takes — the keyword-only parameter on\n`review_plan` in `__init__.py:199`, `overlap` riding beside `probe` at\n`production_batch_runner.py:120-124`, `gate_dispatch.produce_plan_review_verdict` as the\nmiddle link, the new `overlap:` input in `plan-review.yaml`, and the\n`project.plan-overlap` entry in `.rebar/criteria_routing.json`. The reviewer saw and\napproved all of it. `.gitignore` is the one file the plan does not name: it un-ignores the\nnew project-local prompt so the prompt is tracked, following the entries already there for\nthe other `.rebar/prompts` criteria.\n\nfile_impact is now set to the 12 paths that actually landed, each with the reason it was\ntouched. Widening is a material plan change, so the plan-review attestation is invalidated\nand `review-plan` is re-running against the merged tree before the close is retried. No\n`--force`."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793720539273326988,"uuid":"13c4cb50-060a-4fb2-a732-891972da8f6a"}